{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You're in the hospital now because you came in with fever, back pain, and abdominal pain. We’re concerned this might be another kidney infection, especially given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve had this pain for days. It’s worse than usual. And I haven’t been peeing much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s concerning. Your labs show your kidney function is worse—creatinine is 7.2, which is high for you. We think there might be a blockage preventing urine from draining properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? I just had surgery for that. Why does this keep happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s frustrating. The ultrasound shows severe swelling in both kidneys, worse on the left. We suspect a stricture—narrowing—at the connection between your conduit and the left ureter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what are you going to do about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start antibiotics right away for infection. Tomorrow, we’ll do a loopogram—a test where we inject dye into your stoma to see where the blockage is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want any more tubes. Last time it hurt like hell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But without draining the kidney, the infection won’t get better, and your kidneys could be damaged. We’ll use medication to keep you comfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Fine. But I’m not taking any IV meds you push on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2144-08-24 21:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll respect your choices. But I want you to know the antibiotics are important. We’re starting meropenem and daptomycin based on your last infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2144-08-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We placed a catheter into your stoma this morning to help drain urine. You’re making a bit more now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2144-08-25 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It burns. And I still feel pressure in my back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2144-08-25 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected for now. The loopogram today will help us see if there’s a blockage on the left side. If so, interventional radiology may place a tube directly from the kidney out through the skin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2144-08-25 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A tube coming out of my back? No way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2144-08-25 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s temporary. It will help your kidney drain and heal. Without it, the infection could get worse and lead to sepsis again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2144-08-25 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just tell me what the test shows first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2144-08-26 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The loopogram shows the right side is draining fine, but we can’t see the left collecting system. That means there’s likely a blockage at the connection. Radiology recommends a left nephrostomy tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2144-08-26 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s confirmed. Do what you have to do, but I want it out as soon as possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2144-08-26 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll plan for it tomorrow. In the meantime, your urine culture grew Pseudomonas and Enterococcus. Meropenem won’t work for this Pseudomonas, so we’re switching to gentamicin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2144-08-26 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another antibiotic? I’m tired of all these drugs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2144-08-26 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s a lot. But Pseudomonas is tough and resistant to many antibiotics. Gentamicin is one of the few that works, based on the culture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2144-08-27 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nephrostomy was placed successfully. There’s a tube now draining your left kidney into a bag. You should start feeling better as the pressure drops."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2144-08-27 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It hurts. And I hate seeing that bag."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2144-08-27 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given pain meds. The good news is your creatinine is already starting to drop—from 7.2 to 6.1. That means your kidney is recovering."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2144-08-27 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So when can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2144-08-27 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. You still have a fever and high white count. You need at least two weeks of IV antibiotics. We’ll likely place a PICC line for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2144-08-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood work shows your acid levels were very low when you came in—pH 7.18. That’s why you felt so sick. We gave IV bicarbonate, and it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2144-08-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What caused that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2144-08-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A mix of kidney failure and the infection. As your kidneys improve, your body should balance itself. We’ll switch to oral bicarbonate for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2144-08-29 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is down to 18, and you’re afebrile. That’s progress. The nephrostomy is draining well—over 500 mL yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2144-08-29 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I stop the IV meds now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2144-08-29 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We need to finish the full course. We’re also starting subcutaneous epoetin for your anemia, since your hemoglobin is low at 7.8."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2144-08-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound of your arms today to check veins for a PICC line. Your left basilic vein is good—so we’ll place it there tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2144-08-31 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PICC line is in and working. You’ll get gentamicin through it twice a day. We’ll monitor your levels to avoid kidney damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2144-08-31 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long will I need this thing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2144-08-31 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "About two weeks. Then we’ll remove it before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2144-09-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is now 4.0—much better. The nephrostomy is doing its job. Soon, we may replace the tube with a stent inside the body."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2144-09-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That means no more bag?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2144-09-01 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. The stent goes from kidney to bladder or conduit. It drains internally. But we’ll need another procedure to place it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2144-09-02 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—the stent was placed successfully. The tube is out, and the stent is draining into your bag for now. Soon, we’ll cap it to see if urine flows naturally."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2144-09-02 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the bag stays for now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2144-09-02 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, temporarily. Once we confirm the stent works, we’ll cap it and you’ll urinate through your stoma again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2144-09-03 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We capped the stent this morning. You’re still making good urine through your stoma—about 700 mL in 24 hours. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2144-09-03 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2144-09-03 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Almost. Your infection markers are improving, but we need to finish the antibiotics. The PICC will stay until your last dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2144-09-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your WBC is 17.4 and creatinine is 3.5—close to your baseline. The PICC line will be removed tomorrow. You’re on track for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2144-09-04 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What about my pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2144-09-04 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home on oxycodone 60 mg every 8 hours, same as before. We recommend follow-up with pain management to consider long-acting options."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2144-09-04 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to change. This works."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2144-09-04 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We respect that. But please discuss it with your doctor later. You also need urology follow-up in 3 months to exchange the stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2144-09-04 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my skin sores?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2144-09-04 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve kept the dressing clean. Continue daily care at home. See plastic surgery if it worsens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your PICC line is out, labs are stable, and you’re infection-free. You’re cleared for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Finally. What do I need to watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Watch for fever, chills, back pain, or decreased urine. If any occur, come back immediately. Get your labs checked with your PCP soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Urology will contact you for a stent exchange in 3 months. Keep the site clean and monitor output."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try to stay out of here for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do our best to help you. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your urine tested positive for cocaine. For your health, we strongly recommend avoiding it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’m working on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Support is available. Let your team know if you want help. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your meds and discharge papers now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, ready when she is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All the best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hopefully not too soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Ha! Stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2144-09-05 08:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2144-09-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2144-09-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, doc."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2144-08-24 21:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2144-09-05 16:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted with fever, abdominal pain, and back pain, concerning for pyelonephritis and acute on chronic kidney injury, with a creatinine of 7.2. Imaging and a loopogram revealed a left ureteral obstruction causing severe hydronephrosis. A left percutaneous nephrostomy was placed for drainage, leading to improvement in renal function. Urine cultures grew Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Enterococcus, prompting a switch from meropenem to gentamicin. He completed a two-week course of IV antibiotics via a PICC line, which was removed prior to discharge. A nephroureteral stent was placed to maintain drainage, and the patient was transitioned to oral pain medications. He was discharged home in stable condition with plans for urology follow-up and stent exchange in three months.",
    "problems": [
      "Pyelonephritis, unspecified",
      "Left ureteral obstruction",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Metabolic acidosis",
      "Chronic kidney disease, Stage IV (severe)",
      "Neurogenic bladder NOS",
      "Other artificial opening of urinary tract status",
      "Anemia in chronic kidney disease",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Cocaine abuse, unspecified",
      "Opioid abuse, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
